NAME
    snapshot - capture a memory space's full contents

SYNOPSIS
    snapshot <space> <name>
    snapshot list
    snapshot remove <name>

DESCRIPTION
    Saves <space>'s entire current contents under <name> for later 'diff'
    against a further-along state - the general-purpose counterpart to
    'search' when the interesting addresses aren't already narrowed down.
    Same live-hardware-space refusal as 'search'/'dump'.

EXAMPLES
    snapshot WRAM before
    diff before
